WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.581
Step 1. Open the valueset list.

1.2
00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.468
You can select a new valueset when you configure a questionnaire.

1.3
00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:11.201
In Settings, under Forms, select ValueSets.

2.1
00:00:11.201 --> 00:00:13.861
Step 2. Start a new valueset.

2.2
00:00:13.861 --> 00:00:19.681
Select Create ValueSet, and Care opens the Create ValueSet page.

3.1
00:00:19.681 --> 00:00:26.186
Step 3. Choose a starting point. Leave Parent value set empty to start from scratch,

3.2
00:00:26.186 --> 00:00:31.675
or select a valueset to build on. Keep Separate value set selected.

4.1
00:00:31.675 --> 00:00:37.717
Step 4. Enter the basic information. Enter the Name, and Care fills in the Slug.

4.2
00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:41.989
The slug must not match a valueset in the Shared catalogue,

4.3
00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:45.385
and you cannot change it after you save.

5.1
00:00:45.385 --> 00:00:47.315
Step 5. Add the rules.

5.2
00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:52.051
Under Definition, add the include rules and the exclude rules.

5.3
00:00:52.051 --> 00:01:00.156
You can also save a valueset without rules.

6.1
00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:04.119
Step 6. Preview the codes. This step is optional.

6.2
00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:08.635
Select Preview to see the codes that match the rules.

7.1
00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:12.027
Step 7. Save the valueset. Select Save.

7.2
00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:18.553
A new valueset stays hidden, even from you, until it is shared with a department,

7.3
00:01:18.553 --> 00:01:22.920
so Care shows Not Found. Your valueset is saved.
